  "description": "The Nua Luna Pinion is a versatile titanium flat-bar bike built for commuting, bikepacking, and light touring. Designed as a true do-everything platform, it combines Nua’s handcrafted Grade 9 titanium frame with the balanced performance and durability of a Pinion gearbox system. Clean, quiet, and highly adaptable, it’s made for riders who want a refined, low-maintenance bike for everyday riding and extended mixed-terrain adventures. The frame delivers the smooth, resilient ride quality titanium is known for while remaining responsive under load. Practical details include mounts for racks, mudguards, and bottles, internal cable routing, and sliding dropouts for precise belt tension and flexible drivetrain setups. Built around real-world versatility, the Luna transitions easily from daily commuting to weekend exploration and loaded trips. The mechanically actuated Pinion gearbox offers a wide, evenly spaced gear range with consistent performance in all weather conditions. Paired with a Gates Carbon Belt Drive, it provides a clean and durable transmission system designed for long service intervals and dependable use across varied terrain. The frame supports both 650B wheels up to 57 mm for comfort and off-road capability, or 700C wheels up to 44 mm for efficient urban and touring performance. The front end can be configured with either the Nua Carbon Adventure fork for lightweight efficiency or the Nua Titanium Type A fork for a fully titanium build. Stable geometry and a tapered headtube ensure confident handling whether commuting, carrying loads, or riding long mixed-surface routes. Available as a frameset or complete build, the Nua Luna Pinion is a durable, adaptable titanium bike designed for riders who value simplicity, balanced performance, and long-term reliability.",
